1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,646
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,819 --> 00:00:30,280
[Mercedes] <i>The police raided</i>
<i>Club Dragonfly.</i>

6
00:00:30,363 --> 00:00:32,157
<i>They were able to arrest our staff,</i>

7
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,409
<i>confiscate all our profits,</i>
<i>and close down the club.</i>

8
00:00:34,492 --> 00:00:36,536
[Helena] <i>Tell our connections</i>
<i>in the police force</i>

9
00:00:36,619 --> 00:00:40,123
<i>to make sure your name isn't linked</i>
<i>to the club in any way.</i>

10
00:00:40,206 --> 00:00:42,876
[Anna] <i>How can we trust you</i>
<i>when you're keeping secrets from us?</i>

11
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:45,503
<i>Do we still have your loyalty,</i>
<i>or is it with her?</i>

12
00:00:45,587 --> 00:00:47,422
<i>Anna, you are my family.</i>
<i>You, Lily… We're family.</i>

13
00:00:47,505 --> 00:00:48,506
<i>What kind of question is that?</i>

14
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:49,632
<i>You're hiding something from me.</i>

15
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:51,509
<i>I know you've met your mother.</i>

16
00:00:51,593 --> 00:00:53,094
[Apollo] <i>Madam, have mercy on me.</i>

17
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:56,014
[Helena] <i>That's what I want to do</i>
<i>to my new enemies.</i>

18
00:00:56,097 --> 00:00:58,892
<i>Because fire melts gold.</i>

19
00:00:58,975 --> 00:01:01,352
<i>I want to burn Lily Cruz alive!</i>

20
00:01:01,436 --> 00:01:04,105
[Damian] <i>You have no idea</i>
<i>how vicious your enemies are.</i>

21
00:01:04,189 --> 00:01:05,690
<i>But I'm here.</i>

22
00:01:05,774 --> 00:01:07,942
<i>I will protect you from Red Dragon,</i>

23
00:01:08,026 --> 00:01:09,569
<i>even if it kills me.</i>

24
00:01:09,652 --> 00:01:11,780
[Mercedes] <i>Can we still trust Jaguar?</i>

25
00:01:11,863 --> 00:01:15,116
<i>He might betray us because</i>
<i>our enemies are related to him.</i>

26
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,576
<i>I don't trust him at all.</i>

27
00:01:16,659 --> 00:01:17,827
<i>Let me introduce you.</i>

28
00:01:17,911 --> 00:01:21,706
<i>Lily Cruz, meet Helena Montoya,</i>
<i>CEO of Montoya Industries.</i>

29
00:01:21,790 --> 00:01:22,832
<i>It's nice to meet you.</i>

30
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:25,543
[Lily] <i>Poblacion Ardiente needs</i>
<i>people like you.</i>

31
00:01:25,627 --> 00:01:26,669
<i>What are you proposing?</i>

32
00:01:26,753 --> 00:01:28,379
<i>I'm going to have a charity event</i>

33
00:01:28,463 --> 00:01:31,758
<i>to kick-start Oplan Restore</i>
<i>Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

34
00:01:31,841 --> 00:01:33,051
[Jose] <i>You have a visitor.</i>

35
00:01:33,134 --> 00:01:35,011
<i>I'm back. Well and alive.</i>

36
00:01:35,678 --> 00:01:38,598
<i>The time has come for you</i>
<i>to know the whole truth.</i>

37
00:01:38,681 --> 00:01:40,266
<i>You liar! You cheated on me!</i>

38
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:42,060
<i>No! Please! I'm pregnant.</i>

39
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:43,478
-[gunshot]
-[Helena] <i>He killed my father</i>

40
00:01:43,561 --> 00:01:45,063
<i>and separated us.</i>

41
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:47,315
<i>The time has come for my revenge.</i>

42
00:01:47,398 --> 00:01:52,779
[Julio] <i>Those who play with fire,</i>
<i>with Julio Ardiente, will burn!</i>

43
00:01:56,616 --> 00:01:59,035
Just because I'm no longer governor,

44
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:02,122
doesn't mean it's the end of all
our business transactions!

45
00:02:02,205 --> 00:02:03,331
Remember that!

46
00:02:04,332 --> 00:02:05,708
Everyone, get out.

47
00:02:07,836 --> 00:02:10,421
I said, everyone, get out!

48
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:13,133
Sanggano, leave us.

49
00:02:15,969 --> 00:02:19,139
My dearest Papa, you and I
have a lot to talk about.

50
00:02:19,722 --> 00:02:21,516
You took me away from my real mother

51
00:02:21,599 --> 00:02:24,310
and made her think I was dead.
How could you do that?!

52
00:02:25,854 --> 00:02:30,441
Emilia, my dear, please don't
exaggerate your stories.

53
00:02:30,733 --> 00:02:32,902
You act as if I treated you like garbage.

54
00:02:32,986 --> 00:02:36,114
If I had, you would've been
abandoned in some dumpster!

55
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:38,199
But you never treated me
like your daughter!

56
00:02:38,283 --> 00:02:40,952
You even love Arnaldo
more than you love me.

57
00:02:41,035 --> 00:02:42,036
[laughs]

58
00:02:43,371 --> 00:02:46,416
So now you're jealous of your own son?!

59
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:50,420
See?! See how much of a brat you are?

60
00:02:51,546 --> 00:02:53,172
Let's get one thing clear.

61
00:02:53,882 --> 00:02:57,802
I never treated you indifferently.

62
00:02:57,886 --> 00:02:59,178
I never abused you!

63
00:03:00,263 --> 00:03:01,973
I let you live in a palace.

64
00:03:02,056 --> 00:03:05,184
I provided you with the best education

65
00:03:05,268 --> 00:03:06,644
money could buy!

66
00:03:06,728 --> 00:03:08,062
I gave you everything.

67
00:03:08,146 --> 00:03:11,232
I even gave you governorship
of this province

68
00:03:11,316 --> 00:03:12,650
once upon a time!

69
00:03:12,942 --> 00:03:16,571
Yes. You're right, Papa.
You gave me everything.

70
00:03:17,113 --> 00:03:19,699
But you never gave me the chance
to be with my real mother,

71
00:03:19,782 --> 00:03:21,618
and nothing can replace that!

72
00:03:21,701 --> 00:03:24,037
But she found me, she never gave up on me!

73
00:03:24,370 --> 00:03:27,206
And that's what real love is. Unlike you!

74
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:29,375
You are so selfish, Papa.

75
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:32,503
And now that she's found me,
she's going to make me queen.

76
00:03:32,587 --> 00:03:33,755
And nothing can stop that,

77
00:03:33,838 --> 00:03:36,716
not even you, the great Julio Ardiente!

78
00:03:36,799 --> 00:03:38,509
[tense music playing]

79
00:03:46,976 --> 00:03:49,229
Your mother was a harlot!

80
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:53,942
Darn!

81
00:03:54,609 --> 00:03:55,693
[exhales]

82
00:03:57,153 --> 00:03:58,154
Emilia, wait.

83
00:03:58,238 --> 00:03:59,364
What now?!

84
00:04:00,865 --> 00:04:02,784
What was that I heard you and your dad

85
00:04:02,867 --> 00:04:03,952
were talking about downstairs?

86
00:04:04,035 --> 00:04:05,119
About your real mother?

87
00:04:05,203 --> 00:04:07,580
Grab a newspaper,
and get with the program.

88
00:04:07,914 --> 00:04:09,332
Emilia, that's why I'm asking you.

89
00:04:09,415 --> 00:04:12,835
So, why don't you just tell me
about these things,

90
00:04:12,919 --> 00:04:14,879
instead of telling other people?!

91
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:16,756
Well, you can't really blame me, Raul.

92
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:19,467
It's much easier
talking to others than you.

93
00:04:20,134 --> 00:04:21,761
Hold on, Emilia.

94
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:25,056
Why do you always
have to walk out when we fight?

95
00:04:25,139 --> 00:04:27,183
Can't we just talk like husband and wife?

96
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:28,893
What's there to talk about?

97
00:04:30,728 --> 00:04:32,689
Don't you plan to introduce me to Mommy?

98
00:04:32,772 --> 00:04:34,565
[scoffs] Mommy?!

99
00:04:34,857 --> 00:04:37,110
Why don't you go prove your worth first?

100
00:04:37,193 --> 00:04:39,320
I don't want you making a fool out of me!

101
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:42,198
And, by the way, you aren't
invited to the event, okay?

102
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:43,283
So, go do something else.

103
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:45,243
Like, go to the gym, or whatever.

104
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:53,876
[tense music playing]

105
00:04:59,257 --> 00:05:01,301
[phone ringing]

106
00:05:04,971 --> 00:05:06,055
Hello, Mama?

107
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:08,016
[Helena] Hello, Emilia, darling.

108
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,060
So, have you spoken to your father?

109
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:14,856
Yes, Mama. He's still
the same old, prideful man,

110
00:05:14,939 --> 00:05:19,110
with no hint of regret
for all the mistakes he's done.

111
00:05:19,193 --> 00:05:21,946
You know, I don't think
he's ever going to change.

112
00:05:22,405 --> 00:05:26,326
Well, you have to be patient,
my dear. Remember…

113
00:05:26,409 --> 00:05:27,952
<i>we can still use him.</i>

114
00:05:28,661 --> 00:05:31,205
I want him to attend the charity event

115
00:05:31,289 --> 00:05:34,500
so I can show him
how the pros get it done.

116
00:05:34,584 --> 00:05:36,002
Wait, Mama. Are you gonna give me a hint

117
00:05:36,085 --> 00:05:37,962
on what's about to happen?

118
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:41,466
Well, let's just say that…

119
00:05:41,966 --> 00:05:45,970
I'm going to blind the people
of Ardiente with diamonds.

120
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:48,556
Diamonds?

121
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:53,061
Yes, I'm going to donate 20
million pesos worth of diamonds

122
00:05:53,144 --> 00:05:55,021
to the people of Ardiente.

123
00:05:55,104 --> 00:05:58,691
[laughs] Twenty million pesos
worth of diamonds?

124
00:05:58,775 --> 00:06:01,652
Wow. That's a lot, Mama.

125
00:06:01,736 --> 00:06:03,988
I'm so excited to go to that event.

126
00:06:04,072 --> 00:06:05,823
I can't wait to see you there.

127
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:09,577
-Bye.
-See you.

128
00:06:12,747 --> 00:06:16,334
Hmm… Twenty million pesos
worth of diamonds.

129
00:06:16,417 --> 00:06:17,502
Wow.

130
00:06:26,135 --> 00:06:27,095
Lily.

131
00:06:27,470 --> 00:06:28,429
Mom.

132
00:06:30,973 --> 00:06:32,517
Lily, are you sure we're going

133
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:35,228
to that Helena Montoya's charity event?

134
00:06:36,604 --> 00:06:38,689
We have to, Mom.

135
00:06:38,773 --> 00:06:40,608
But what if it's just a trap?

136
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:43,694
I've already beefed up security.

137
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:47,198
I won't let any of us get hurt
at that charity event.

138
00:06:47,490 --> 00:06:49,283
But we have to go there

139
00:06:49,367 --> 00:06:54,539
so I can find out
who Helena Montoya really is.

140
00:06:54,914 --> 00:06:57,875
There, we'll find out her true identity.

141
00:06:58,251 --> 00:07:02,088
And that's when I'll find out
whether she's my enemy

142
00:07:02,171 --> 00:07:03,422
or my ally.

143
00:07:04,048 --> 00:07:06,717
[suspenseful music playing]

144
00:07:11,973 --> 00:07:15,852
[waltz music playing]

145
00:07:29,866 --> 00:07:32,952
[waltz music playing]

146
00:07:46,382 --> 00:07:48,259
[waltz music playing]

147
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:01,689
[music fading]

148
00:08:04,442 --> 00:08:06,944
Get ready because we have another mission.

149
00:08:07,028 --> 00:08:09,030
A certain package will arrive

150
00:08:09,238 --> 00:08:11,616
at Helena Montoya's charity event.

151
00:08:11,699 --> 00:08:14,952
Diamonds worth 20 million pesos.

152
00:08:16,204 --> 00:08:18,706
But it won't reach the charity event

153
00:08:19,248 --> 00:08:20,875
because we'll take them all.

154
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:22,710
Understood?

155
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:24,462
Understood, Boss Jaguar.

156
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:32,887
Oh, Jaguar. You're not late.

157
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:35,181
You're on time, huh? [chuckles]

158
00:08:37,141 --> 00:08:40,603
I have a job for you. Get your men ready.

159
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:45,274
Protect the diamonds
I've sent for the charity event.

160
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:47,985
Make sure that they get there.

161
00:08:48,277 --> 00:08:49,946
[distorted voice]
As you wish, Madam Red Dragon.

162
00:08:50,655 --> 00:08:51,739
Very good.

163
00:08:54,575 --> 00:08:56,577
[suspenseful music playing]

164
00:09:01,207 --> 00:09:04,085
[waltz music playing]

165
00:09:13,803 --> 00:09:16,472
[waltz music playing]

166
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:39,287
-This way, please.
-Thank you.

167
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,628
We should stay here.

168
00:09:48,045 --> 00:09:50,756
[waltz music playing]

169
00:09:59,056 --> 00:10:00,683
They're here.

170
00:10:01,976 --> 00:10:04,103
[suspenseful music playing]

171
00:10:09,942 --> 00:10:11,569
-[usherette] This way, ma'am.
-Okay.

172
00:10:13,195 --> 00:10:14,989
Excuse me, ma'am. Name, please.

173
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:17,241
My name's Natalie.

174
00:10:17,325 --> 00:10:18,367
Surname?

175
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:23,539
Well, about that.
I actually invited myself.

176
00:10:24,081 --> 00:10:25,958
I'm sure there's nothing wrong with that.

177
00:10:26,834 --> 00:10:30,880
I want to meet the wealthiest jeweler

178
00:10:30,963 --> 00:10:33,466
in all of Southeast Asia.

179
00:10:34,091 --> 00:10:35,301
Can you make it happen?

180
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:40,765
I'm sorry, ma'am, but this event
is strictly by invitation.

181
00:10:40,848 --> 00:10:41,932
[chuckles]

182
00:10:42,308 --> 00:10:47,104
Darling, why don't you do both
of us a favor and let me in.

183
00:10:47,355 --> 00:10:48,856
I'm a VIP, you know.

184
00:10:48,939 --> 00:10:50,107
-VIP?!
-I'm sorry, ma'am,

185
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:52,568
-[laughs]
-but you have to leave.

186
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:54,654
You're so right, you're a VIP.

187
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:56,697
Very immoral person.

188
00:10:56,781 --> 00:11:00,785
[laughs] That's so witty. I like it a lot!

189
00:11:00,868 --> 00:11:03,621
And guess what? It suits you too.

190
00:11:03,704 --> 00:11:06,374
Because it takes one to know one.

191
00:11:06,832 --> 00:11:08,709
Emilia, look at me.

192
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:12,380
I'm not in a chair,
and I'm not tied to it.

193
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:14,632
Which means it's payback time.

194
00:11:14,965 --> 00:11:17,635
Enough of these confrontation scenes.

195
00:11:17,718 --> 00:11:19,637
I'm sick of them!

196
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:22,139
-[grunts]
-Oops! Not too fast.

197
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:24,725
Come on. Take her out. Pronto.

198
00:11:24,809 --> 00:11:27,603
-[Natalie] Let me go! Hey!
-Crazy.

199
00:11:27,686 --> 00:11:28,687
[grunts]

200
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:32,149
[Natalie] Let me go!

201
00:11:33,692 --> 00:11:36,487
[tense music playing]

202
00:11:37,947 --> 00:11:39,073
Hmm!

203
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:44,495
If it isn't Ivy Aguas.

204
00:11:44,578 --> 00:11:46,414
Or is it Lily Cruz?

205
00:11:46,997 --> 00:11:49,375
[sighs] I'm so confused. Who are you?

206
00:11:50,167 --> 00:11:52,628
But all I know is you, little witch,

207
00:11:52,711 --> 00:11:53,879
are invited to this party.

208
00:11:53,963 --> 00:11:55,131
But don't you worry

209
00:11:55,214 --> 00:11:59,552
because I will deal with the other witch.

210
00:11:59,927 --> 00:12:00,970
Really?

211
00:12:01,762 --> 00:12:04,598
[laughs] Yes. I will deal with you.

212
00:12:04,682 --> 00:12:07,685
One, two, three. It's a reunion!

213
00:12:07,768 --> 00:12:09,061
This is so fun.

214
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:11,939
I'm going to have so much fun
with these three little witches.

215
00:12:12,022 --> 00:12:14,191
Let me deal with that witch.

216
00:12:14,275 --> 00:12:15,234
Wow.

217
00:12:15,317 --> 00:12:19,113
Apparently, it slipped her mind
that I haven't forgotten

218
00:12:19,196 --> 00:12:21,282
that she buried me alive.

219
00:12:23,617 --> 00:12:28,706
Lily Cruz, why are you
wearing green and not gold?

220
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:31,375
What happened to that gold outfit?

221
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:32,293
[laughs]

222
00:12:32,376 --> 00:12:35,880
Oh, no. Has Lily Cruz lost her luster?

223
00:12:37,047 --> 00:12:41,177
You know what, Emilia?
They say gold glitters.

224
00:12:41,802 --> 00:12:44,805
But not all that glitters is gold.

225
00:12:45,473 --> 00:12:47,057
I am gold.

226
00:12:48,142 --> 00:12:52,188
But you, and you…

227
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:56,817
Just look at yourselves.

228
00:12:57,568 --> 00:12:59,987
I'd say you're just copper.

229
00:13:00,070 --> 00:13:02,031
I don't even know what that is.

230
00:13:02,114 --> 00:13:03,240
You shut up.

231
00:13:03,324 --> 00:13:08,120
But in all fairness to you, Natalie,
no matter where you are in Ardiente,

232
00:13:08,204 --> 00:13:09,246
you're always in the know.

233
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:16,170
Lily Cruz? Ivy Aguas?

234
00:13:16,253 --> 00:13:19,048
They are the same person.

235
00:13:19,131 --> 00:13:20,466
And that's me.

236
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:26,472
Well, I've no time for chatting
with people like you.

237
00:13:26,555 --> 00:13:27,723
And you, Emilia…

238
00:13:30,226 --> 00:13:33,896
Starting today,
you should fear for your life.

239
00:13:35,523 --> 00:13:38,150
Because not only will I bury you alive,

240
00:13:38,234 --> 00:13:40,903
I'll make your life a living hell.

241
00:13:42,196 --> 00:13:43,906
[chuckles]

242
00:13:43,989 --> 00:13:45,658
For now, maybe.

243
00:13:45,741 --> 00:13:47,952
But in a while,

244
00:13:48,911 --> 00:13:53,415
I'll make you wish you had never
left your old casket, Lily Cruz.

245
00:13:53,499 --> 00:13:55,209
[laughing]

246
00:13:55,543 --> 00:13:58,879
You may have tried to bury us
both back then,

247
00:13:59,421 --> 00:14:02,841
but what else should we expect
from a she-demon like you?

248
00:14:02,925 --> 00:14:04,552
[laughing]

249
00:14:04,802 --> 00:14:07,096
-Wait. Wow!
-[Natalie laughing]

250
00:14:07,179 --> 00:14:09,014
There are now four witches.

251
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:13,894
One, two, three, four.
The more the merrier. I love it.

252
00:14:13,978 --> 00:14:15,688
I love it! This is gonna be so exciting!

253
00:14:15,771 --> 00:14:16,772
We're gonna fight,

254
00:14:16,855 --> 00:14:18,232
-and I'll pull your hair.
-Hey, you.

255
00:14:18,315 --> 00:14:20,150
-And your hair.
-And why are you laughing, huh?

256
00:14:20,234 --> 00:14:22,236
You think I don't know why you're here?

257
00:14:22,319 --> 00:14:25,030
You're here to seduce
my husband again, aren't you?

258
00:14:25,114 --> 00:14:28,868
[laughs] That's so last month.
I've moved on.

259
00:14:28,951 --> 00:14:33,038
I've squeezed everything
I needed out of your husband.

260
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:35,416
I mean, information, that is.

261
00:14:36,208 --> 00:14:41,922
So, now, who could my new flavor
of the month be?

262
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:45,175
Or should I address that to you?

263
00:14:45,843 --> 00:14:48,387
Wanna take a guess, Lily Cruz?

264
00:14:49,054 --> 00:14:51,974
Take a wild guess.

265
00:14:57,980 --> 00:14:59,189
Who cares?

266
00:15:02,359 --> 00:15:04,403
[laughing]

267
00:15:07,656 --> 00:15:10,200
-[laughs]
-Hmm…

268
00:15:13,412 --> 00:15:15,748
[Natalie] I'm so confused.

269
00:15:16,916 --> 00:15:21,378
You might go crazy when you find out who.

270
00:15:25,883 --> 00:15:27,468
Lily Cruz!

271
00:15:27,885 --> 00:15:29,970
[tense music playing]

272
00:15:43,692 --> 00:15:47,613
[tense music playing]

273
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:56,246
[Natalie laughs]

274
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,087
You can turn your backs on me.

275
00:16:03,170 --> 00:16:06,423
I don't really care 'cause
none of you can take me on.

276
00:16:06,507 --> 00:16:07,508
Especially not you.

277
00:16:07,591 --> 00:16:11,220
Because you're a sore loser,
Emilia! Loser!

278
00:16:11,303 --> 00:16:12,888
-Really?
-Yes.

279
00:16:13,305 --> 00:16:15,766
Girls, please escort this little birdbrain

280
00:16:15,849 --> 00:16:16,809
out of here.

281
00:16:16,892 --> 00:16:19,561
-I can walk! What?!
-And do her a good job.

282
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:21,230
-[woman] Good job?
-Yes. Kill her!

283
00:16:21,313 --> 00:16:23,607
You're such a loser, Emilia!

284
00:16:23,691 --> 00:16:26,902
[laughs] I'll see you in hell. Take care.

285
00:16:27,319 --> 00:16:28,320
[Natalie] Let me go!

286
00:16:28,404 --> 00:16:29,780
-Oh! I love it!
-[Natalie grunts]

287
00:16:31,365 --> 00:16:33,283
[jazz music playing]

288
00:16:34,952 --> 00:16:35,995
[Lily] Anna.

289
00:16:39,581 --> 00:16:42,835
[host] May I request everyone
to please settle down?

290
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:45,629
[jazz music playing]

291
00:16:53,095 --> 00:16:55,681
[jazz music playing]

292
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:01,562
[groans]

293
00:17:03,313 --> 00:17:05,649
[jazz music playing]

294
00:17:07,443 --> 00:17:10,654
Hi, Lily Cruz, my favorite adversary.

295
00:17:10,738 --> 00:17:11,864
How are you?

296
00:17:11,947 --> 00:17:15,617
So, are you ready to compete against me

297
00:17:15,701 --> 00:17:18,454
in earning Helena Montoya's favor?

298
00:17:19,496 --> 00:17:20,622
[chuckles]

299
00:17:20,706 --> 00:17:24,001
Emilia, I don't need
to compete against you.

300
00:17:24,501 --> 00:17:25,794
Did you honestly forget?

301
00:17:25,878 --> 00:17:27,629
I already beat you.

302
00:17:28,964 --> 00:17:31,216
And I don't want to make a scene

303
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:34,428
because I came here
to create ties with Helena

304
00:17:34,511 --> 00:17:36,764
for Ardiente's citizens.

305
00:17:36,847 --> 00:17:38,057
So, please.

306
00:17:39,516 --> 00:17:41,226
So, you honestly believe

307
00:17:41,310 --> 00:17:44,772
that Helena Montoya
wants a partnership with you?

308
00:17:45,105 --> 00:17:47,024
Pretty cocky, aren't you?

309
00:17:47,316 --> 00:17:49,485
Anyway, everything will
be revealed tonight,

310
00:17:49,568 --> 00:17:51,278
although it might be too much for you.

311
00:17:52,071 --> 00:17:53,363
Your jaw might just drop.

312
00:17:54,114 --> 00:17:55,157
Try me.

313
00:18:02,414 --> 00:18:03,749
Careful with that.

314
00:18:09,505 --> 00:18:10,506
Just follow them.

315
00:18:10,589 --> 00:18:13,217
[Helena] <i>Thank you all very much</i>
<i>for coming.</i>

316
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:15,135
Thank you very much.

317
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:18,430
I would especially like
to thank Lily Cruz…

318
00:18:19,056 --> 00:18:22,017
for coming this evening
and supporting this event.

319
00:18:22,101 --> 00:18:24,144
-Thank you, Lily.
-[mouths] You're welcome.

320
00:18:26,355 --> 00:18:28,565
I bet many of you are wondering

321
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:31,276
why I chose to help Poblacion Ardiente,

322
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:33,320
of all places.

323
00:18:34,238 --> 00:18:39,618
But many of you don't know that
I have memories of this place,

324
00:18:39,701 --> 00:18:43,997
which is why I chose
to build a better future here.

325
00:18:44,790 --> 00:18:48,919
Poblacion Ardiente is my home.

326
00:18:50,462 --> 00:18:52,756
Because my family lives here.

327
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:58,887
Ladies and gentlemen,
I would like to introduce to you

328
00:18:59,304 --> 00:19:01,515
my long-lost daughter…

329
00:19:01,849 --> 00:19:03,892
[tense music playing]

330
00:19:09,314 --> 00:19:11,984
Emilia Ardiente-Torillo!

331
00:19:12,359 --> 00:19:16,738
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[applause]

332
00:19:22,452 --> 00:19:23,662
Mama.

333
00:19:23,745 --> 00:19:26,582
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[applause]

334
00:19:38,093 --> 00:19:40,012
-[applause]
-[soft music playing]

335
00:19:56,486 --> 00:19:59,448
-[applause]
-[soft music playing]

336
00:20:17,883 --> 00:20:20,469
-I love you, Mama.
-I love you, baby girl.

337
00:20:24,014 --> 00:20:26,475
To those of you asking,
"How did this happen?"

338
00:20:27,184 --> 00:20:30,896
Oh, it's such a long story.
We don't have the whole night.

339
00:20:32,147 --> 00:20:33,815
But as you all know,

340
00:20:34,483 --> 00:20:38,779
I endeavor to empower women and mothers.

341
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:40,656
And for the longest time,

342
00:20:40,739 --> 00:20:43,158
I have been a champion of mothers.

343
00:20:43,951 --> 00:20:47,287
But what most of you might not know…

344
00:20:48,372 --> 00:20:52,084
is that I'm also a mother
who's been looking for her child

345
00:20:52,709 --> 00:20:54,294
for so long.

346
00:20:54,962 --> 00:20:57,965
But that all ends here tonight.

347
00:21:00,217 --> 00:21:03,387
Today, I am proud to announce

348
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:08,433
that I am finally reunited
with my beloved daughter.

349
00:21:10,894 --> 00:21:14,898
And no one, not even the demon himself,

350
00:21:14,982 --> 00:21:16,650
can tear us apart.

351
00:21:26,451 --> 00:21:27,452
I love you, Mama.

352
00:21:27,536 --> 00:21:29,079
I love you, baby girl.

353
00:21:29,162 --> 00:21:31,456
Once again, the philanthropist,

354
00:21:31,540 --> 00:21:33,292
the successful businesswoman…

355
00:21:33,375 --> 00:21:37,045
Hail to the queen. Helena Montoya!

356
00:21:37,129 --> 00:21:39,047
[applause]

357
00:21:42,634 --> 00:21:45,429
-[applause]
-[tense music playing]

358
00:21:58,650 --> 00:22:02,154
-[applause]
-[tense music playing]

359
00:22:17,085 --> 00:22:20,422
-[applause]
-[tense music playing]

360
00:22:28,305 --> 00:22:30,098
[suspenseful music playing]

361
00:22:31,266 --> 00:22:34,478
Get that away from me.
I think I might steal it.

362
00:22:36,646 --> 00:22:38,106
An egg.

363
00:22:39,191 --> 00:22:41,610
That's how big your brain is.

364
00:22:42,069 --> 00:22:43,945
As big as a quail egg!

365
00:22:45,363 --> 00:22:48,283
Do you want Red Dragon
to cut off your fingers?

366
00:22:48,617 --> 00:22:52,746
We were ordered to deliver
and protect her diamonds.

367
00:22:53,121 --> 00:22:55,665
Only an idiot would betray Red Dragon.

368
00:22:57,959 --> 00:23:00,545
Boss, someone's following us.

369
00:23:05,425 --> 00:23:08,512
Boss, looks like we have company.

370
00:23:11,056 --> 00:23:12,099
We do.

371
00:23:13,517 --> 00:23:14,810
The fake Jaguar.

372
00:23:18,188 --> 00:23:19,564
Step on it, buzz-cut.

373
00:23:23,110 --> 00:23:24,820
[distorted voice] Faster. Hurry.

374
00:23:27,447 --> 00:23:28,907
I said, faster!

375
00:23:28,990 --> 00:23:30,784
[tires screeching]

376
00:23:31,326 --> 00:23:32,452
Get ready.

377
00:23:35,497 --> 00:23:37,666
[tires screeching]

378
00:23:38,041 --> 00:23:39,251
Get ready.

379
00:23:40,961 --> 00:23:43,505
-[gunshots]
-[tires screeching]

380
00:23:51,346 --> 00:23:52,472
[Damian] Get down.

381
00:23:53,265 --> 00:23:55,976
[suspenseful music playing]

382
00:24:06,903 --> 00:24:08,780
Give us the diamonds,

383
00:24:09,114 --> 00:24:12,284
and we promise we'll let you pass.

384
00:24:12,951 --> 00:24:14,286
[softly] You've got a screw loose.

385
00:24:14,703 --> 00:24:16,913
These are Red Dragon's diamonds.

386
00:24:17,581 --> 00:24:21,168
Blood will be spilled
before I give these to you.

387
00:24:21,251 --> 00:24:24,254
[suspenseful music playing]

388
00:24:31,428 --> 00:24:32,554
All right then.

389
00:24:34,347 --> 00:24:37,475
[gunshots]

390
00:24:42,230 --> 00:24:43,523
[gunshots]

391
00:24:44,399 --> 00:24:45,400
[Damian] Retreat!

392
00:24:45,483 --> 00:24:46,526
[Raul] Check it out!

393
00:24:48,153 --> 00:24:49,196
[Raul] Corner them!

394
00:24:51,531 --> 00:24:53,074
[Raul] Grab the diamonds! Quick!

395
00:24:57,829 --> 00:24:59,080
[Raul] Give me that thing! Give it here!

396
00:24:59,164 --> 00:25:00,040
[Damian] Hey!

397
00:25:01,249 --> 00:25:02,709
[explosion]

398
00:25:04,211 --> 00:25:07,797
[Raul groaning]

399
00:25:08,089 --> 00:25:10,634
[Damian] Get those creaky bodies moving

400
00:25:10,717 --> 00:25:12,260
if you don't want to be beaten,

401
00:25:12,344 --> 00:25:15,430
stop sleeping there like helpless kittens!

402
00:25:15,972 --> 00:25:16,973
Hey, that rhymed!

403
00:25:17,057 --> 00:25:19,226
[laughs mockingly]

404
00:25:19,309 --> 00:25:20,560
I'm a poet!

405
00:25:22,938 --> 00:25:24,189
Get the diamond.

406
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:29,736
[grunts]

407
00:25:37,202 --> 00:25:39,663
[grunts, groans]

408
00:25:40,288 --> 00:25:41,331
[grunts]

409
00:25:45,835 --> 00:25:46,836
[groans]

410
00:25:49,339 --> 00:25:50,757
[Raul] Quit acting like you're all that.

411
00:25:50,840 --> 00:25:52,300
You're just another lackey!

412
00:25:52,384 --> 00:25:54,094
[Damian laughs mockingly]

413
00:25:54,427 --> 00:25:56,680
Why don't you look at yourself,
little kitten?

414
00:25:57,430 --> 00:26:00,267
Fake little Jaguar here became a has-been.

415
00:26:02,477 --> 00:26:03,812
Too bad!

416
00:26:04,938 --> 00:26:08,316
You better practice first,
if you want to get a punch in!

417
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:10,402
[laughs mockingly]

418
00:26:10,485 --> 00:26:13,196
It still rhymed! Come on, boys!

419
00:26:14,698 --> 00:26:16,950
[suspenseful music playing]

420
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:19,536
[engine turns over]

421
00:26:34,134 --> 00:26:36,761
[suspenseful music playing]

422
00:26:44,477 --> 00:26:47,731
[Helena] And now,
let's go to the main event.

423
00:26:49,274 --> 00:26:52,068
[suspenseful music playing]

424
00:27:01,786 --> 00:27:06,916
I would like to present
my biggest diamond collection.

425
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:17,135
The Phoenix! For Poblacion Ardiente.

426
00:27:17,385 --> 00:27:19,637
-[applause]
-[tense music playing]

427
00:27:37,364 --> 00:27:39,866
-[applause]
-[tense music playing]

428
00:27:52,962 --> 00:27:55,965
-[applause]
-[tense music playing]

429
00:27:59,010 --> 00:28:00,053
[eerie music]

430
00:28:16,694 --> 00:28:18,988
So Emilia is Helena Montoya's daughter?

431
00:28:23,076 --> 00:28:23,993
[Mr. Castro] <i>Miss Cruz.</i>

432
00:28:24,077 --> 00:28:25,495
<i>We need to set a meeting with you</i>

433
00:28:25,578 --> 00:28:27,163
<i>and Mrs. Helena Montoya.</i>

434
00:28:27,247 --> 00:28:29,249
<i>She's the CEO of Montoya Industries.</i>

435
00:28:29,332 --> 00:28:30,625
<i>She made a great offer.</i>

436
00:28:30,875 --> 00:28:32,168
[Mateo] <i>She's the most successful jeweler</i>

437
00:28:32,252 --> 00:28:34,587
<i>in the Philippines, and she's</i>
<i>willing to share her fortunes</i>

438
00:28:34,671 --> 00:28:35,880
<i>with the people of Ardiente.</i>

439
00:28:35,964 --> 00:28:37,132
[Lily] <i>The same Helena Montoya</i>

440
00:28:37,215 --> 00:28:39,259
<i>who wants to invest in my company.</i>

441
00:28:39,634 --> 00:28:40,760
<i>That's me.</i>

442
00:28:40,844 --> 00:28:42,554
<i>Let's help each other.</i>

443
00:28:42,971 --> 00:28:45,557
<i>Together, we can help</i>
<i>the people of Ardiente</i>

444
00:28:45,640 --> 00:28:47,517
<i>rise from the ashes.</i>

445
00:28:49,352 --> 00:28:54,482
Now I know why she wants
to get close to me.

446
00:28:56,359 --> 00:28:58,194
She's planning something against you.

447
00:29:00,321 --> 00:29:02,031
It's obvious, Diego.

448
00:29:04,159 --> 00:29:06,077
But what Helena's doing?

449
00:29:07,078 --> 00:29:08,913
She's taking a page from Ivy Aguas' book.

450
00:29:09,581 --> 00:29:13,209
<i>I want to be part of Ardiente's progress.</i>

451
00:29:13,293 --> 00:29:16,880
<i>An auction whose profits will go</i>
<i>to the campaign fund</i>

452
00:29:16,963 --> 00:29:18,590
<i>of our congressman.</i>

453
00:29:18,673 --> 00:29:23,094
<i>I hope this is the start</i>
<i>of our partnership.</i>

454
00:29:23,178 --> 00:29:26,806
<i>For Poblacion Ardiente! Cheers!</i>

455
00:29:29,517 --> 00:29:31,227
She has no originality.

456
00:29:31,936 --> 00:29:33,146
But, oh well…

457
00:29:33,229 --> 00:29:38,735
If that's what she wants,
the show must go on.

458
00:29:39,235 --> 00:29:42,071
[tense music playing]

459
00:29:44,157 --> 00:29:47,869
Helena, I love your whole collection.

460
00:29:47,952 --> 00:29:48,787
Thank you.

461
00:29:48,870 --> 00:29:51,956
But aren't they all
too precious to be donated?

462
00:29:52,582 --> 00:29:55,585
Precious diamonds for this precious town?

463
00:29:55,668 --> 00:29:58,505
Only my new hometown deserves the best.

464
00:29:58,963 --> 00:30:02,842
See? That's my Mama. Isn't she nice?

465
00:30:03,134 --> 00:30:04,427
And she can fund it,

466
00:30:04,511 --> 00:30:07,222
unlike you and Diego Torillo's project.

467
00:30:07,722 --> 00:30:09,724
You'll only pale in comparison.

468
00:30:10,934 --> 00:30:11,976
[clears throat]

469
00:30:12,227 --> 00:30:14,896
Oh, Helena, don't mind your daughter.

470
00:30:14,979 --> 00:30:16,481
She's always been like that.

471
00:30:16,773 --> 00:30:18,525
So, please be patient with her.

472
00:30:19,275 --> 00:30:20,401
But as for me,

473
00:30:20,902 --> 00:30:23,863
I will never compete with you. Never.

474
00:30:25,573 --> 00:30:27,158
Lily, please believe me when I say

475
00:30:27,242 --> 00:30:29,953
I only have good intentions for this town.

476
00:30:30,328 --> 00:30:32,330
As a matter of fact,
I've already thought of

477
00:30:32,413 --> 00:30:33,581
so many projects.

478
00:30:33,665 --> 00:30:35,291
Why don't you join me

479
00:30:35,375 --> 00:30:37,460
in my latest project for the town?

480
00:30:37,544 --> 00:30:39,796
Sure, Helena. Sure.

481
00:30:39,879 --> 00:30:42,423
This conversation stinks.

482
00:30:42,715 --> 00:30:43,716
Excuse me?

483
00:30:45,718 --> 00:30:47,387
Well, you know, I must admit,

484
00:30:47,470 --> 00:30:50,056
you both are very good actresses.

485
00:30:50,682 --> 00:30:52,600
To be able to stand each other

486
00:30:52,684 --> 00:30:54,686
and not get at each other's throats?

487
00:30:55,103 --> 00:30:57,605
My, I'll give you an A for effort.

488
00:30:58,398 --> 00:31:00,733
Although as much as I hate the guts

489
00:31:00,817 --> 00:31:03,903
of this woman in green, she's right.

490
00:31:04,779 --> 00:31:06,739
Those diamonds are only beautiful

491
00:31:06,823 --> 00:31:09,617
to a fool who thinks
they don't come with a price.

492
00:31:13,204 --> 00:31:15,290
You're staging a comeback, Helena.

493
00:31:15,915 --> 00:31:18,376
And you want to take over my town?

494
00:31:18,877 --> 00:31:21,212
[chuckles, tutting]

495
00:31:21,921 --> 00:31:22,964
Julio.

496
00:31:24,299 --> 00:31:27,927
I truly want to help this town, yes.

497
00:31:28,970 --> 00:31:30,722
But I won't force you.

498
00:31:31,681 --> 00:31:35,685
Because only a fool thinks
that he can change the mind

499
00:31:35,768 --> 00:31:37,395
of another fool.

500
00:31:37,645 --> 00:31:40,315
[Julio] Wow. She thinks.

501
00:31:40,607 --> 00:31:42,275
Why don't we all raise our glasses?

502
00:31:42,984 --> 00:31:46,571
After all, we all want
the best for our town.

503
00:31:47,280 --> 00:31:48,865
-[Emilia] Yeah.
-[taps on glass]

504
00:31:49,324 --> 00:31:50,950
Onward, Ardiente!

505
00:31:51,034 --> 00:31:54,329
Um, Mama, it's Viva Ardiente!

506
00:31:55,163 --> 00:31:57,373
-Viva Ardiente!
-Nice!

507
00:31:57,749 --> 00:31:58,708
[Mateo] Viva Ardiente!

508
00:32:00,752 --> 00:32:03,421
[tense music playing]

509
00:32:10,887 --> 00:32:13,973
[suspenseful music playing]

510
00:32:25,193 --> 00:32:27,612
[suspenseful music playing]

511
00:32:36,371 --> 00:32:38,498
[suspenseful music playing]

512
00:32:52,220 --> 00:32:54,847
[suspenseful music playing]

513
00:33:06,818 --> 00:33:09,362
[soft music playing]

514
00:33:25,586 --> 00:33:26,713
[Jepoy] <i>I'll go with you.</i>

515
00:33:27,380 --> 00:33:28,464
[Anna] <i>Why?</i>

516
00:33:29,132 --> 00:33:31,300
<i>Doesn't your girl need you now?</i>

517
00:33:32,719 --> 00:33:34,846
[Jepoy] <i>First of all,</i>
<i>Natalie's not my girl.</i>

518
00:33:35,972 --> 00:33:37,015
<i>Second…</i>

519
00:33:37,098 --> 00:33:39,600
<i>I'll go with you to protect you.</i>

520
00:33:40,727 --> 00:33:42,061
<i>Please believe me.</i>

521
00:33:42,937 --> 00:33:45,231
<i>I'll prove that you have my loyalty.</i>

522
00:33:48,651 --> 00:33:49,694
[line ringing]

523
00:33:51,821 --> 00:33:52,822
[line ringing]

524
00:33:57,118 --> 00:34:00,121
Anna. Where's Jepoy?

525
00:34:00,371 --> 00:34:01,831
He suddenly left, Auntie Camia.

526
00:34:01,914 --> 00:34:04,667
I'm trying to call him,
but he won't answer.

527
00:34:04,959 --> 00:34:06,836
I don't know where he went.

528
00:34:06,919 --> 00:34:11,382
-[line ringing]
-[suspenseful music playing]

529
00:34:18,139 --> 00:34:21,934
Let me go! [grunts]

530
00:34:22,018 --> 00:34:24,312
Why are you two so strong?!
You're so tiny!

531
00:34:24,479 --> 00:34:26,314
[grunts]

532
00:34:27,607 --> 00:34:29,984
[shrieks, whimpers]

533
00:34:30,359 --> 00:34:31,986
What kind of trick is that?

534
00:34:32,070 --> 00:34:33,488
It's so tacky!

535
00:34:33,571 --> 00:34:35,865
-Are you guys crazy?
-This isn't a trick!

536
00:34:35,948 --> 00:34:37,658
This is what will burn you alive!

537
00:34:37,742 --> 00:34:39,410
Madam Emilia says goodbye.

538
00:34:39,494 --> 00:34:41,287
What does that wretch even think she is?!

539
00:34:41,370 --> 00:34:42,663
[shrieks, whimpers]

540
00:34:42,747 --> 00:34:44,749
Is this a circus? Are we at a festival?

541
00:34:44,832 --> 00:34:47,126
Can you just stop this nonsense?!

542
00:34:50,129 --> 00:34:51,214
What's that?

543
00:34:52,173 --> 00:34:53,341
Uh, excuse me!

544
00:34:54,217 --> 00:34:56,219
[panting] No!

545
00:34:56,302 --> 00:34:59,138
[breathing raggedly]

546
00:35:00,431 --> 00:35:01,516
Stop it!

547
00:35:01,849 --> 00:35:03,434
Can you stop?! [shrieks]

548
00:35:04,310 --> 00:35:06,479
Stop! Ugh!

549
00:35:06,938 --> 00:35:08,356
How do you even swallow this?!

550
00:35:08,439 --> 00:35:09,607
This is disgusting!

551
00:35:11,317 --> 00:35:13,027
[suspenseful music playing]

552
00:35:20,952 --> 00:35:23,204
-Hey, let her go!
-Madrigal!

553
00:35:27,375 --> 00:35:28,417
Whoa!

554
00:35:31,379 --> 00:35:37,385
-[henchwoman screams]
-[Jepoy, henchwomen grunting]

555
00:35:41,305 --> 00:35:42,348
I'm serious!

556
00:35:45,226 --> 00:35:46,227
Let her go!

557
00:35:49,397 --> 00:35:50,439
Ladies first, I guess.

558
00:35:51,149 --> 00:35:52,567
-[screams]
-[grunts]

559
00:35:53,484 --> 00:35:54,569
[screams]

560
00:35:55,653 --> 00:36:01,242
[grunting, groaning]

561
00:36:04,579 --> 00:36:05,621
Back off!

562
00:36:07,623 --> 00:36:08,916
-Yay!
-Ma'am!

563
00:36:09,167 --> 00:36:11,294
Madrigal, thank you so much!

564
00:36:11,377 --> 00:36:13,254
[Jepoy] Why did you crash
the event in the first place?

565
00:36:13,337 --> 00:36:14,380
Are you crazy?!

566
00:36:15,590 --> 00:36:16,674
I'm sorry.

567
00:36:17,216 --> 00:36:18,342
Let's go.

568
00:36:18,843 --> 00:36:20,178
I knew you'd save me.

569
00:36:20,887 --> 00:36:21,929
[squeals]

570
00:36:22,430 --> 00:36:23,472
[grunts]

571
00:36:25,224 --> 00:36:26,309
Thank you.

572
00:36:26,851 --> 00:36:27,894
[squeals]

573
00:36:29,437 --> 00:36:30,271
Thank you.

574
00:36:30,354 --> 00:36:31,564
You're lucky I found you.

575
00:36:31,647 --> 00:36:32,648
[smooches]

576
00:36:37,778 --> 00:36:39,488
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

577
00:36:44,619 --> 00:36:45,661
[Emilia scoffs]

578
00:36:46,370 --> 00:36:48,873
The next time you cross over my Mama,

579
00:36:49,498 --> 00:36:51,459
I will crush you like a fly.

580
00:36:51,751 --> 00:36:52,877
[exhales]

581
00:36:52,960 --> 00:36:54,629
Go ahead, Emilia.

582
00:36:55,087 --> 00:36:58,674
You know what?
All you do is bark and bark.

583
00:36:58,758 --> 00:37:02,470
But you keep hiding behind
your mother's skirt

584
00:37:02,845 --> 00:37:05,556
because you can't handle me.

585
00:37:05,848 --> 00:37:08,684
You and I are mortal enemies.
And you know that.

586
00:37:09,810 --> 00:37:13,105
You also know that when a child
sees their mother hurt,

587
00:37:13,189 --> 00:37:14,523
they'll do something about it.

588
00:37:14,982 --> 00:37:17,860
So, keep my mother out of this. Okay?

589
00:37:17,944 --> 00:37:19,779
Because no one's been declared the victor

590
00:37:19,862 --> 00:37:21,822
in our fight yet. Get that?

591
00:37:21,906 --> 00:37:23,658
Just accept it, Emilia.

592
00:37:23,741 --> 00:37:27,078
Accept your loss, Emilia.

593
00:37:27,495 --> 00:37:29,830
Because I already won.

594
00:37:30,790 --> 00:37:31,958
And don't worry.

595
00:37:32,041 --> 00:37:33,834
I won't drag your mother into this.

596
00:37:34,460 --> 00:37:37,713
But, please, don't get jealous.

597
00:37:37,797 --> 00:37:41,008
Because I already feel a sense
of connection with your mother.

598
00:37:41,092 --> 00:37:43,970
I just know we're going to be close.

599
00:37:44,262 --> 00:37:45,346
Excuse me.

600
00:37:45,930 --> 00:37:47,056
Hmm!

601
00:37:47,139 --> 00:37:48,474
You witch!

602
00:37:50,059 --> 00:37:52,853
[tense music playing]

603
00:37:52,937 --> 00:37:53,938
Hmm.

604
00:38:01,195 --> 00:38:03,656
Lily, I don't trust that Helena.

605
00:38:03,948 --> 00:38:06,784
Who would give away diamonds
just like that?

606
00:38:08,744 --> 00:38:11,122
If she just wanted to be with Emilia…

607
00:38:12,415 --> 00:38:14,875
she didn't have to make a grand show

608
00:38:14,959 --> 00:38:16,460
announcing the whole thing.

609
00:38:17,003 --> 00:38:20,589
She's doing all this to get close to you.

610
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:24,010
All I'm going to do with Helena…

611
00:38:25,970 --> 00:38:28,681
is dance to her tune.

612
00:38:29,140 --> 00:38:30,266
But Lily…

613
00:38:31,976 --> 00:38:33,019
Be wary.

614
00:38:33,769 --> 00:38:35,688
You don't know who you're up against.

615
00:38:36,355 --> 00:38:39,233
Protect yourself. Don't level with her.

616
00:38:43,195 --> 00:38:49,493
Mom, my plan is to wait and see
just what she'll do to me.

617
00:38:51,704 --> 00:38:57,376
They may have buried Ivy Aguas,
but her words still remain.

618
00:38:58,461 --> 00:39:03,215
So to Emilia and Helena… don't try me.

619
00:39:03,841 --> 00:39:06,552
[suspenseful music playing]

620
00:39:20,941 --> 00:39:22,902
Why did you have to make a scene?

621
00:39:23,861 --> 00:39:25,112
Aren't you smarter than that?

622
00:39:25,196 --> 00:39:28,074
And no mother would let a lunatic like you

623
00:39:28,157 --> 00:39:29,200
hurt their child!

624
00:39:30,368 --> 00:39:31,952
You're lucky I was there.

625
00:39:32,036 --> 00:39:34,372
If you'll just rub it
in my face that you saved me,

626
00:39:34,455 --> 00:39:37,083
I wish you didn't even save me anymore!

627
00:39:37,166 --> 00:39:40,211
I don't need you! I can manage!

628
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:43,214
Try telling yourself that!
If I didn't come…

629
00:39:43,839 --> 00:39:44,882
Then what?

630
00:39:45,383 --> 00:39:47,093
I already saved you before.

631
00:39:47,176 --> 00:39:50,179
And thank you for saving me!
Now, we're even!

632
00:39:50,429 --> 00:39:51,680
Now, you can just go!

633
00:39:51,889 --> 00:39:53,933
Why don't you just go and leave me?!

634
00:39:55,976 --> 00:39:57,019
Leave!

635
00:40:02,191 --> 00:40:03,818
What are you staring at?!

636
00:40:16,372 --> 00:40:17,415
Ma'am…

637
00:40:20,459 --> 00:40:21,752
just be careful.

638
00:40:25,131 --> 00:40:26,632
I don't want this happening again.

639
00:40:45,067 --> 00:40:46,360
[gasps]

640
00:40:52,074 --> 00:40:53,367
I had so much fun tonight, Mama.

641
00:40:53,451 --> 00:40:55,870
I love that on you. It's so beautiful.

642
00:40:55,953 --> 00:40:56,954
Thank you.

643
00:40:58,789 --> 00:41:03,502
Now, that move was low
even for you, Helena.

644
00:41:04,253 --> 00:41:05,296
[sighs]

645
00:41:05,379 --> 00:41:08,632
Which one? The diamonds I gave to charity?

646
00:41:08,716 --> 00:41:12,720
The ones you gave me months
before you left me,

647
00:41:13,220 --> 00:41:14,763
and took away my daughter?

648
00:41:16,724 --> 00:41:19,310
Julio, it's just a constant reminder

649
00:41:19,393 --> 00:41:22,771
of the monster that you are
and will always be.

650
00:41:23,772 --> 00:41:24,940
So what?

651
00:41:25,649 --> 00:41:28,194
You returned to reunite

652
00:41:28,277 --> 00:41:31,489
with your long-lost daughter to spite me?

653
00:41:31,572 --> 00:41:34,241
I'm not here for
petty sentimentalities, Julio.

654
00:41:34,325 --> 00:41:37,203
I'm here to help my daughter
achieve her ambitions.

655
00:41:39,121 --> 00:41:42,082
You use your force, and I use my charm.

656
00:41:42,166 --> 00:41:43,292
[scoffs]

657
00:41:43,375 --> 00:41:46,879
And my charm is going to cloak
the violent force

658
00:41:46,962 --> 00:41:49,131
that's gonna annihilate my enemy.

659
00:41:49,924 --> 00:41:50,966
You're in luck.

660
00:41:52,301 --> 00:41:53,969
We share the same enemy.

661
00:41:54,929 --> 00:41:57,473
So, why don't you just sit back and relax,

662
00:41:57,556 --> 00:42:01,143
and watch me bleed Lily Cruz to death?

663
00:42:01,602 --> 00:42:06,190
[speaking in Spanish] The enemy
of my enemy is my friend.

664
00:42:08,609 --> 00:42:09,860
-Bye.
-Bye, Mama.

665
00:42:13,405 --> 00:42:14,573
[scoffs]

666
00:42:18,077 --> 00:42:21,330
Your mother hasn't changed one bit.

667
00:42:22,081 --> 00:42:25,376
She's still the feisty woman I knew.

668
00:42:26,377 --> 00:42:32,841
Man-eater, destroyer, firecracker.

669
00:42:36,845 --> 00:42:37,846
[clicks tongue]

670
00:42:37,930 --> 00:42:42,393
You know, Papa, I can see in your eyes

671
00:42:42,476 --> 00:42:44,979
that you're head
over heels crazy about Mama.

672
00:42:45,062 --> 00:42:46,564
Look at those eyes.

673
00:42:46,647 --> 00:42:47,773
Twinkling.

674
00:42:47,856 --> 00:42:50,484
But eat her dust!

675
00:42:51,068 --> 00:42:53,195
Did you see how she looked at me?

676
00:42:53,445 --> 00:42:54,446
[Emilia humming]

677
00:42:54,530 --> 00:42:55,990
As thick as oil.

678
00:42:56,574 --> 00:42:59,159
Go and join your new master.

679
00:42:59,952 --> 00:43:01,120
[laughs]

680
00:43:01,954 --> 00:43:04,748
I am going to enjoy this.

681
00:43:04,832 --> 00:43:06,709
[upbeat music playing]

682
00:43:15,050 --> 00:43:16,802
[art dealer] It's the same, actually.

683
00:43:17,261 --> 00:43:19,597
Miss Montoya follows a certain rate.

684
00:43:19,680 --> 00:43:23,183
So, there's a price ceiling.
So, we can't just…

685
00:43:26,145 --> 00:43:27,354
Sir, excuse me, please.

686
00:43:31,400 --> 00:43:32,484
Hi, ma'am. Good morning.

687
00:43:33,444 --> 00:43:35,195
This installation is made
of precious stones

688
00:43:35,279 --> 00:43:37,197
like jade, diamond, and amethyst.

689
00:43:37,281 --> 00:43:39,074
A personal offer of Miss Montoya.

690
00:43:43,329 --> 00:43:44,288
It's beautiful.

691
00:43:46,707 --> 00:43:50,919
But isn't Mrs. Montoya a jewelry maker?

692
00:43:51,170 --> 00:43:54,298
Well, she also creates mixed media arts

693
00:43:54,381 --> 00:43:56,133
featuring women rising from tragedies,

694
00:43:56,216 --> 00:43:59,428
metamorphosis, blossoming flowers…

695
00:44:00,262 --> 00:44:01,889
butterflies, and phoenixes,

696
00:44:02,306 --> 00:44:03,807
as you can see in the installation.

697
00:44:07,269 --> 00:44:08,771
I'll get that and this one.

698
00:44:09,855 --> 00:44:13,067
And I want to send a note to Miss Montoya.

699
00:44:13,150 --> 00:44:14,193
Sure, ma'am.

700
00:44:15,235 --> 00:44:19,531
Oh, um, would you know
where I can find her?

701
00:44:19,615 --> 00:44:22,201
[suspenseful music playing]

702
00:44:27,790 --> 00:44:30,209
[piano music playing]

703
00:44:30,793 --> 00:44:32,961
Paula, make an appointment
for Mrs. Harper.

704
00:44:33,045 --> 00:44:35,506
Tell her that she needs to fit her tiara.

705
00:44:35,923 --> 00:44:37,591
Madam, someone wants to talk to you.

706
00:44:38,384 --> 00:44:39,760
I don't have an appointment today.

707
00:44:41,303 --> 00:44:42,805
[Paula] Um, ma'am.

708
00:44:42,888 --> 00:44:44,473
[tense music playing]

709
00:44:44,556 --> 00:44:45,557
[Paula] Excuse me.

710
00:44:48,060 --> 00:44:49,937
[suspenseful music playing]

711
00:44:57,653 --> 00:44:59,863
[Helena] <i>If you loathe them,</i>
<i>why are you here?</i>

712
00:44:59,947 --> 00:45:01,323
<i>Am I now your enemy too?</i>

713
00:45:01,407 --> 00:45:03,659
<i>Or is it because</i>
<i>you're planning to use me?</i>

714
00:45:03,742 --> 00:45:08,163
<i>Is that also why you haven't</i>
<i>declared war against me, Helena?</i>

715
00:45:08,247 --> 00:45:09,373
[Mercedes] <i>Have you started?</i>

716
00:45:09,456 --> 00:45:12,960
<i>Or should I just kill you</i>
<i>together with Camia and Lily?</i>

717
00:45:13,043 --> 00:45:18,006
<i>Helena Montoya is somehow</i>
<i>connected to Mercedes Palacio.</i>

718
00:45:18,090 --> 00:45:21,927
<i>How can there be a reunion</i>
<i>when my grandson isn't here?</i>

719
00:45:22,010 --> 00:45:23,011
<i>Let me go! Let me go!</i>

720
00:45:23,095 --> 00:45:24,513
[Helena] <i>Diego is a thorn.</i>

721
00:45:24,596 --> 00:45:26,682
<i>So if you don't do something</i>
<i>about it tonight,</i>

722
00:45:26,765 --> 00:45:30,310
<i>then you are the biggest thorn</i>
<i>in this family!</i>

723
00:45:30,811 --> 00:45:33,689
[theme music playing]
